  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Follow up CGIAR</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Uppdrag f&#xF6;r uppf&#xF6;ljning CGIAR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Givet omfattningen av det svenska st&#xF6;det och givet Sveriges betydande roll inom CGIAR, finns behov av expertkunskap inom CGIAR reformen och deras nya styrsystem, givare koordination genom den europeiska givare grupp till CGIAR (EIARD) samt erfarenhet av CGIARs System Council, st&#xF6;d f&#xF6;r uppf&#xF6;ljning i CGIAR System Council samt deltagande i f&#xF6;rberedande m&#xF6;ten inom EIARD. Insatsen bidrar till att ge expertst&#xF6;d genom anlitande av konsult.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det svenska st&#xF6;det till internationell jordbruksforskning som bedrivs inom CGIAR-systemet har p&#xE5;g&#xE5;tt sedan 1973 och &#xE4;r omfattande med en volym om 664 MSEK under &#xE5;ren 2013 - 2017. Ett nytt st&#xF6;d planeras fr&#xE5;n 2018 och volymen f&#xF6;r detta ber&#xE4;knas bli minst 115 MSEK per &#xE5;r. 
Sverige har, genom Sida, r&#xF6;str&#xE4;tt i CGIARs System Council. System Council best&#xE5;r av representanter av givare och utvecklingsl&#xE4;nder och fattar beslut om f&#xF6;rdelning av medel till forskningsprogrammen inom CGIARn&#xE4;tverket.
De europeiska givarna, eller representanter f&#xF6;r dessa, tr&#xE4;ffas i The European Initiative for Agricultural Research for Development (EIARD) f&#xF6;r att f&#xF6;rbereda diskussionen inf&#xF6;r System Council. 
P&#xE5; grund av omfattningen av det svenska st&#xF6;det och givet Sveriges betydande roll inom CGIAR, finns behov av expertkunskap inom CGIAR reformen och deras nya styrsystem, givare koordination genom den europeiska givare grupp till CGIAR (EIARD) samt erfarenhet av CGIARs System Council, Detta behov ska t&#xE4;ckas genom konsultst&#xF6;d f&#xF6;r uppf&#xF6;ljning i CGIAR System Council samt deltagande i f&#xF6;rberedande m&#xF6;ten inom EIARD under 2018.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The international agricultural research though the CGIAR-system has been supported by Sida since 1973. The amount of the support has been 664 MSEK during 2013 &#x2013; 2017. The preparation of a new agreement from 2018 has started and the agreed amount is expected to be at least 115 MSEK/year.
Sweden has, through Sida, a vote in the CGIAR System Council. CGIAR System Council consists of representatives of donors and members of developing countries. The System Council decides on the distribution of support to the different research programmes within the system.
The European donors, or representatives of those, meet in The European Initiative for Agricultural Research for Development (EIARD) to prepare for the discussions in the System Council.
Due to the complexity of the Swedish support and Sweden&#x2019;s important role in CGIAR, there is a need of expert knowledge of the CGIAR reform and its new management system, donor coordination through EIARD and experience of CGIAR System Council. This contribution will cover this need through expert support for follow-up in the System Council and participation in EIARD during 2018.</narrative>
  </description>
